WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
- So, what did you love about the city?

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.629
You've been here for years.
- Yeah.

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:03.470
- So what was... When
you first moved here,

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.930
what was like, your favorite thing to do?

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.330
- Well, I mean, I think that,
like a lot of New Yorkers,

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.890
you just can't believe like,
how close everything is.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.970
Like, every cuisine you'd ever want to try

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.620
is just a block away.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.750
And it's also the great
thing about New York,

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.060
is that people behave exactly the way

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.210
you always hoped New Yorkers would.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.043
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:23.580
I remember like, early on like,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.090
one of my first days running to SNL

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.100
and I had a script in
like a Manila envelope

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.790
and an unstapled script
and it just blew away.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.210
And people were walking,

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.970
not a single person stopped to help me,

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.871
but a lot of them pointed
where the paper was going.

00:00:40.871 --> 00:00:42.029
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:42.970
They would be on their phone

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.210
and they'd just go, "There,
it's in the street".

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.740
- New York is full of supervisors.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.150
- [Seth] Yeah, just a lot of like, people.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.367
And also, people always say like,

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.900
"Do you get stopped, as a celebrity,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.580
do you get stopped in New York much?"

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.900
And I always say you don't,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.360
because everyone who lives in New York

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.109
thinks they're a celebrity.

00:00:58.109 --> 00:00:58.942
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:00.278
Like, anybody here.
- That's awesome.

00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:02.300
- [Seth] I think it's great, yeah.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.530
- I was like, that's
amazing, that's amazing.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.363
- When I started,

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:05.930
I remember like, my
first year on the show,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.237
being at a bar in New York
and the bartender said,

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:11.010
"Has anyone told you, you
look like that guy on SNL?"

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.470
And I said... I was so excited,

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.300
because I hadn't been recognized before.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.190
And I said, "I am that guy on SNL".

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.446
And he said, "Shut up".

00:01:17.446 --> 00:01:18.580
(audience laughs)

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.455
- That totally happens
to me, still to this day.

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:21.410
- Do people think you
look like Kelly Clarkson?

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.360
- 20 years in and I'll
be like, "Oh, I am".

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.350
And they're like, "No you're not".

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.300
And I'm like, "Oh, no, I'm not".

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.267
And then they're like, "Are you?"

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.240
"Yes I am", "No, you're not".

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.210
We have this argument, back and forth

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.950
and then I just give
up and I'm like, "No".

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:33.880
- You know, what you should do is,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.470
you should ask for their name

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.502
and whatever they say,
go, "No, you're not".

00:01:37.502 --> 00:01:38.335
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:40.710
- I'm not as funny as you.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.800
So wait, so it's, it's all
your years here or sorry,

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.570
in all your years, I'm... You guys,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.000
we're going to have to have a fan.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.480
I mean, I am legit,

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.782
I'm going to look like a Guns
N' Roses concert in about 2.2.

00:01:52.782 --> 00:01:53.615
(audience laughs)

00:01:53.615 --> 00:01:54.660
- This is a very... People can't tell

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.253
that this is actually carved
out of a block of ice,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.710
to like self-cool the guests.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.770
- I am like a really, I'm
trying to keep it together.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.380
Okay, it's all like a slip and slide.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:06.490
Okay, okay.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:08.240
So in all your years here,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.800
what's the most like, New York thing

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.090
that you've ever seen happen?

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.730
- Oh gosh, the most New York
thing I've ever happened...

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.540
This well, all right,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.350
can I talk about cockroaches for a second?

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.800
- I'm from Texas, we have huge ones.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:19.633
- [Seth] Okay, gotcha.

00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:21.010
I think the most unique thing

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.970
about New York cockroaches
is when they finally die...

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:25.950
- [Kelly] Which they don't.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.542
- They walk into the
middle of your kitchen.

00:02:28.542 --> 00:02:29.660
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.987
And they do it there, because
they want you to know,

00:02:31.987 --> 00:02:34.773
"I've been here, this whole time".

00:02:34.773 --> 00:02:35.606
(audience cheers)

00:02:35.606 --> 00:02:37.370
- And there's plenty more.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.154
- And there's more, "I'm not here alone".

00:02:41.154 --> 00:02:43.610
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.910
- That's the thing I found out about LA.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.920
So, I'm used to cockroaches from Texas.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.610
We have huge ones, but in LA it's rats.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.443
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:02:50.443 --> 00:02:51.276
- So, I'm just like out in my backyard

00:02:51.276 --> 00:02:54.280
and like a rat, like literally
didn't just run across,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.740
stopped, stared me in the
face and then kept going.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.100
And I was like, where there's
one rat, there's a plethora.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.921
So I'm like, freaking, I'd
take the roaches over rats.

00:03:04.921 --> 00:03:07.900
But one of your writers,
Amber Ruffin, who I love.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:08.975
I love her.

00:03:08.975 --> 00:03:09.852
(audience cheers)

00:03:09.852 --> 00:03:12.530
She joked, she joked that you got Botox.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.940
Wait, wait, wait, before you leave.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.270
Wait, Seth is on my show tomorrow,

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.640
so should I ask him anything?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.140
- Oh yes, there is a very, true rumor

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.479
that Seth got Botox, this summer.

00:03:21.479 --> 00:03:23.319
You should ask him about that.

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:26.119
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:03:26.119 --> 00:03:27.370
- That was a private conversation,

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.430
between me and a writer that

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.170
was not supposed to be on television.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.080
And it's very hurtful to me that...

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.440
I know I'm very, it's a lovely joke,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.180
because I didn't get Botox,

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.920
but my natural skin,

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.989
looks like it's been
stretched over my face.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.440
- Well, that's amazing.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.273
- [Seth] Yeah, I think so too.

00:03:45.273 --> 00:03:46.790
- Congratulations, genetics.
- Thank you very much.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.353
Yeah, yeah, yeah, it's really good.

